    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const d=$input.item.json;\nconst folderUrl=d.drive_folder_url||'';\nconst folderId=d.sub_folder_id||'';\nconst msg='Redesign the graphs from the source blog into AlfredAI-branded infographic graphs, following your full workflow and the AlfredAI blog-graph design system.\\n\\nSOURCE: Read the blog at the link below. Identify each existing graph, chart, or data visual in it. For each one, recreate it as an AlfredAI-branded graph using the skill design system (dark navy #0F1729 background, accent order pink #FF4D8E, cyan #22D3EE, green #4ADE80, purple #8B5CF6, orange #F59E0B; Inter/DejaVu Sans typography; the 6 layout patterns: hub-and-spoke, donut, column cards, timeline, stat grid, split panel). Match each graph to the best layout for its content. Follow the readability and overlap-prevention standards (large readable fonts, no overlapping text, vary layout patterns).\\n\\nFor each graph produce BOTH an editable SVG and a blog-ready PNG.\\n\\nSource blog link:\\n'+d.feed_link+'\\n\\nPRE-SHIP QUALITY CHECK (mandatory - do this BEFORE uploading anything to Google Drive): Before you upload, review every generated graph and verify ALL of the following. Do NOT upload until every item passes; if any fails, fix it and re-render first.\\n1. TEXT CORRECTNESS: all labels, numbers, titles, and legends are accurate to the source data, spelled correctly, and complete. No placeholder text, no cut-off words, no wrong values.\\n2. NO OVERLAP: no text overlaps other text, data points, legends, or graph edges. Labels are fully readable and not colliding. Nothing is clipped.\\n3. READABILITY: fonts are large and legible against the dark navy background with strong contrast. No cramped or tiny text.\\n4. GRAPHICS CORRECT: each graph accurately represents the source chart, uses the correct on-brand colors, is not distorted or duplicated, and the layout pattern fits the data. Data values match the source.\\n5. COMPLETENESS: every graph identified in the source has a corresponding redesigned SVG and PNG; nothing missing.\\nOnly once every check passes, proceed to upload.\\n\\nUPLOAD (MANDATORY - required final step):\\nDESTINATION_FOLDER_ID: '+folderId+'\\nDESTINATION_FOLDER_URL: '+folderUrl+'\\n\\nAfter the quality check passes, you MUST upload every final file (all SVG and PNG graph files) to the user\\'s Google Drive using rclone, targeting the EXISTING destination folder by its ID. Use the rclone flag --drive-root-folder-id '+folderId+' so the files land directly INSIDE that existing folder. The destination is a shared drive, so include shared-drive support. Run the upload EXACTLY ONCE; do not re-run or duplicate. Do NOT create a new folder. Do NOT use the folder ID as a new folder name. Do NOT leave files only in your task workspace. After uploading, confirm in your task output the exact list of files you placed in that folder, and note what each graph shows.';\nreturn{json:{...d,manus_message:msg}};"
      },
